_ZwKd7BGO3wkWPb34_dU058s_rcPUrzyzRn227t83g8a7CBd9zjj-7_67hJl0I47irdLPl7938H_r19--eV__w9mzlLOMmcAAA","summary":{"white":"SeanWinshand","black":"umutataakbas","whiteElo":"3073","blackElo":"3017","result":"1-0","opening":"Lion Defense: Anti-Philidor, Lion's Cave","as":"b","accuracy":{"w":84.8,"b":79.2},"counts":{"w":{"best":36,"miss":1,"blunder":1,"mistake":1,"great":1},"b":{"best":33,"mistake":2,"brilliant":1,"great":1,"blunder":1}},"moment":{"name":"22…Re2","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","fen":"r2q2k1/pp3ppp/2p5/3nB1PP/3P4/2P2N2/P2Qr3/1K1R2R1 w - - 1 23","from":"e4","to":"e2"},"finalFen":"2k5/2R5/2N5/p3B3/P7/1p6/3K4/8 b - - 1 65"},"white":"SeanWinshand","black":"umutataakbas","labels":["book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","good","best","best","excellent","good","excellent","good","inaccuracy","best","best","excellent","good","mistake","inaccuracy","best","inaccuracy","inaccuracy","best","good","good","good","best","good","best","best","best","best","miss","best","inaccuracy","best","best","best","blunder","brilliant","best","best","best","inaccuracy","mistake","best","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","great","excellent","inaccuracy","best","best","best","good","best","blunder","great","best","best","mistake","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","excellent","good","best","excellent","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","excellent","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","excellent","good","best","excellent","excellent","best","excellent","best","good","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","best","best","best","forced","best","best","best","forced","best"],"moments":[{"ply":37,"name":"19.Bxf5","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"19.Bxf5 lets the win slip: 19.gxf6 kept White winning. White's winning chances go from 89% to 70%.","points":["Black answers 19…Ne4: moving away uncovers the queen on d8, which now hits the g5 pawn.","Better was 19.gxf6 (+5.69), which takes the knight on f6."],"better":"19.gxf6 wins a bishop for two pawns and stops …Ne4. After 19…Bxd3+ 20.Qxd3 Nxf6 21.cxb4 Nxh5 22.Rh1, the bishops are traded and White comes out a piece and a pawn up (+5.69)."},{"ply":43,"name":"22.bxc3","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"22.bxc3 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 66% to 41%.","points":["Black answers 22…Re2: the rook reaches the seventh rank, where 1 pawn sits and the king is cut off on the back rank.","Better was 22.Qc2 (+1.81), which attacks the rook on e4, which is undefended."],"better":"22.Qc2 gets the queen out of the way of …Bxd2 and threatens Qxe4, winning a rook for a pawn. After 22…Re3 23.g6 fxg6 24.Rd3 Bb4 25.Rxe3 Nxe3 26.Qd3, the rooks are traded and White is a pawn down (+1.81)."},{"ply":44,"name":"22…Re2","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"22…Re2!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the rook on e2 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: White's best reply is 23.Qc1 Qa5 24.Rd2 Nxc3+ instead (the engine rates it −1.22).","The rook reaches the seventh rank, where 1 pawn sits and the king is cut off on the back rank.","22…Re2 threatens …Rxd2, winning the queen for a rook.","It threatens …Rxd2, winning the queen for a rook, so White has to spend the next move on it.","The rook on e2 can be taken by the queen on d2."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"22…Re2!! offers the rook on e2. Taking it gives Black the material back and more."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"22…Re2 puts the rook on e2 where it can be taken by the queen on d2. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It threatens …Rxd2, winning the queen for a rook."},{"title":"If White takes the rook","text":"23.Qxe2 is met by 23…Nxc3+, taking the c3 pawn with check. Then 24…Nxe2 takes the queen on e2, and 25…Qa5 threatens …Qc3+, winning a rook. Black ends up about a queen's worth of material ahead: Black is winning (−3.91)."},{"title":"White's best try","text":"White's best is to leave the rook alone and play 23.Qc1. Black answers 23…Qa5, threatening …Qxa2# and mate. Then 24…Nxc3+ gives check, and 25…Nxa2 takes the a2 pawn. Black ends up a piece ahead: Black is a little better (−1.22)."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 22…Re3, is clearly weaker (+0.91 against −1.22). White answers 23.c4, attacking the knight on d5. That would leave Black a little worse."}]},{"ply":49,"name":"25.Bxg7+","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"25.Bxg7+ is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 50% to 34%.","points":["Black answers 25…Kxf7, which takes the pawn on f7.","Better was 25.Rxd2 (0.00), which takes the rook on d2."],"better":"25.Rxd2 wins a rook and stops the mate threat …Qb6+. After 25…Qa5 26.c4 Ne3 27.Rf2 Kxf7 28.Rxg7+ Ke8, White comes out the exchange plus a pawn up (0.00)."},{"ply":56,"name":"28…Qd5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"28…Qd5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the h5 pawn, which is undefended.","Protects the knight on e4, which was hanging.","The next best move, 28…Nc3, would drop Black's winning chances from 77% to 29% (+2.40).","28…Qd5 stops Rxe4 and threatens …Qc4+, forking the king and the rook.","White was threatening Rxe4, winning a knight. Qd5 takes care of it.","It threatens …Qc4+, forking the king and the rook, so White has to spend the next move on it."]},{"ply":64,"name":"32…Nxe2","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"32…Nxe2 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 61% to 22%.","points":["White answers 33.Nf4+, which gives check, so the reply is forced.","The knight walks into a pin by the rook on e1.","After Nf4+, White wins 8 points of material within 5 moves.","Better was 32…Kd7 (−1.16): the king steps out of the firing line (fewer enemy pieces aim at it now)."],"better":"32…Kd7 steps the king out of the firing line. After 33.Nc5+ Kc8 34.Re8+ Rxe8 35.Rxe8+ Kc7, the rooks are traded (−1.16)."},{"ply":65,"name":"33.Nf4+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"33.Nf4+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Gives check, so the reply is forced.","The next best move, 33.Nc5+, would drop White's winning chances from 78% to 10% (−5.85).","33.Nf4+ wins the queen for a pawn, picking it up with 34.Nxd5.","Sets up a sequence and wins the queen for a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 34.Nxd5.","Black answers 33…Kd6.","After 33…Kd6 34.Nxd5 Nxd4+ 35.Kd3 Nf3 36.Re3 Kxd5 37.Rxf3 Rd8, White comes out 8 points of material up (+3.31)."]},{"ply":68,"name":"34…Ng3","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"34…Ng3 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 23% to 9%.","points":["White answers 35.Nf6: the knight forks the rook and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","After Nf6, White wins 1 point of material within 4 moves.","Better was 34…Nxd4+ (+3.30), which takes the pawn on d4."],"better":"34…Nxd4+ wins a pawn. After 35.Kd3 Nf3 36.Re3 Kxd5 37.Rxf3 Rd8, Black comes out a pawn up (+3.30)."}],"opening":{"name":"Lion Defense: Anti-Philidor, Lion's Cave","eco":"B07","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 5.Nf3: 9 moves in all, 5 by White and 4 by Black.","Black left the book with 5…exf4. In 533 games from this position, strong players played 5…exd4 (88%), 5…c6 (8%), 5…Be7 (3%) or 5…g6 (under 1%).","The main line goes on 5…exd4 6.Qxd4 c6 7.Be3 d5 8.e5 Ng4 9.Bg1 Bc5 10.Qd2.","From here White scored 53% in those games, with 11% drawn."]}}